1
00:00:06,060 --> 00:00:11,037
Y measurements a couple of the games.

2
00:00:11,120 --> 00:00:12,580
That's symmetric.

3
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:16,130
Yuuuu-Gi-Oh!

4
00:00:16,340 --> 00:00:17,399
Thinking I kill me

5
00:00:18,680 --> 00:00:22,380
You realize what I'm doing

6
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:24,082
Is the trouble?

7
00:00:25,860 --> 00:00:26,690
Yeah

8
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:05,060
So far, all of the evidence
points to your defeat.

9
00:01:06,060 --> 00:01:09,300
I find you guilty of
poor dueling. Oh, yeah?

10
00:01:09,540 --> 00:01:11,580
We'll just see. My move.

11
00:01:12,220 --> 00:01:13,720
All right, what to do?

12
00:01:14,080 --> 00:01:18,557
His face-down card is probably a trap,
but I can't worry about that right now.

13
00:01:18,640 --> 00:01:20,577
I have to get a monster on the field,

14
00:01:20,660 --> 00:01:23,437
or else he'll be able to
attack my life points again.

15
00:01:23,520 --> 00:01:25,720
And I got just a guy for the job.

16
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:27,440
So look out, Johnson.

17
00:01:27,900 --> 00:01:29,477
Now I play this card.

18
00:01:29,560 --> 00:01:31,660
Panther Warrior in attack mode!

19
00:01:34,980 --> 00:01:38,080
And then, I'll place one card face down.

20
00:01:38,360 --> 00:01:41,320
His Cameon Wizard has
only 1,300 attack points,

21
00:01:41,460 --> 00:01:44,737
so my Panther Warrior should be
able to wipe it out with no problem.

22
00:01:44,820 --> 00:01:49,585
But just in case he tries anything funny,
I've got my face down card as a backup.

23
00:01:49,880 --> 00:01:51,300
That's it for me, Judge.

24
00:01:51,640 --> 00:01:53,320
Hmm, you're up to something.

25
00:01:53,580 --> 00:01:55,600
Oh well, I'm not too worried.

26
00:01:56,240 --> 00:01:58,017
Because I have this card.

27
00:01:58,100 --> 00:01:59,300
Ready, Joseph?

28
00:01:59,660 --> 00:02:02,280
Reveal the magic card leading question!

29
00:02:02,660 --> 00:02:05,857
This card adds 800 attack
points to any monster

30
00:02:05,940 --> 00:02:08,717
that's made up of two other
monsters fused together.

31
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:13,040
So my cameon, Wizard, is now
stronger than your panther warrior.

32
00:02:14,260 --> 00:02:16,020
Wizard, attack now!

33
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:18,000
Not so fast, Mr.

34
00:02:18,160 --> 00:02:19,572
Tall, Dark and Gruesome!

35
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:21,560
You've triggered my track!

36
00:02:22,220 --> 00:02:23,680
Go, Skull Dice!

37
00:02:24,700 --> 00:02:28,480
The higher I roll, the more
attack points your monster loses.

38
00:02:29,720 --> 00:02:30,550
Yeah!

39
00:02:32,140 --> 00:02:34,480
Perhaps he should take a closer look.

40
00:02:35,740 --> 00:02:36,570
What?

41
00:02:36,653 --> 00:02:37,483
A one?

42
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:38,480
No way!

43
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:41,120
All right.

44
00:02:41,360 --> 00:02:44,595
I don't know how you did
that, but I got my eye on you.

45
00:02:44,880 --> 00:02:50,180
In my courtroom, twisting the facts is
perfectly legal, especially when it helps me.

46
00:02:52,160 --> 00:02:52,990
No!

47
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:54,320
My Panther Warrior!

48
00:02:54,460 --> 00:02:57,166
Once again, you have no
monsters on the field.

49
00:02:57,280 --> 00:03:01,440
And as for me, you remember my
Sinister Justice card, don't you?

50
00:03:01,660 --> 00:03:04,680
It gives me another 800 life points.

51
00:03:05,880 --> 00:03:07,000
Not again!

52
00:03:07,420 --> 00:03:11,538
That will happen every time my cameon
wizard attacks your life points.

53
00:03:11,640 --> 00:03:12,600
Stop this guy!

54
00:03:12,880 --> 00:03:14,900
You almost had him beat once!

55
00:03:15,080 --> 00:03:17,727
Until he turned things
around and whooped ya.

56
00:03:17,880 --> 00:03:18,717
Gee, thanks.

57
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:20,280
Order in the court.

58
00:03:20,660 --> 00:03:21,880
Make your move.

59
00:03:22,360 --> 00:03:24,297
Jansen's got me right where he wants me.

60
00:03:24,380 --> 00:03:26,677
Thanks to his leading question magic card,

61
00:03:26,760 --> 00:03:29,760
his Cameon Wizard gets a
power boost of 800 points.

62
00:03:29,860 --> 00:03:32,920
That gives it a grand total
of 2100 attack points.

63
00:03:33,140 --> 00:03:37,240
And all I have in my hand is
the Swordsman of Landstar,

64
00:03:37,460 --> 00:03:40,460
who's not exactly what I'd
call a king of monsters.

65
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:42,280
What's the matter?

66
00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:45,117
Did little Joseph use up
all of his best monsters

67
00:03:45,200 --> 00:03:48,000
during the first five
minutes of the duel? No!

68
00:03:48,440 --> 00:03:51,580
The truth is, I did, and
now I'm paying the price.

69
00:03:52,140 --> 00:03:54,580
Well, make your move.

70
00:03:55,160 --> 00:03:56,940
All right, fine, Johnson.

71
00:03:57,680 --> 00:03:59,640
Hey, graceful dice!

72
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:01,300
If my luck improves,

73
00:04:01,580 --> 00:04:04,697
I may be able to raise my Swordsman
of Landstar's attack points.

74
00:04:04,780 --> 00:04:07,040
I summon Swordsman of Landstar!

75
00:04:08,700 --> 00:04:13,020
And then, I'll play
this, my graceful dice!

76
00:04:16,100 --> 00:04:19,500
Yeah, raise my sorceress
attack points with a high roll.

77
00:04:20,560 --> 00:04:22,680
All right, it worked.

78
00:04:23,260 --> 00:04:24,480
Not quite.

79
00:04:29,600 --> 00:04:32,580
What did I do to deserve all this?

80
00:04:32,900 --> 00:04:37,020
I've never seen him have such
terrible luck before. Poor Joey.

81
00:04:39,380 --> 00:04:42,217
Oh, Joseph, that's my move now.

82
00:04:42,300 --> 00:04:45,160
Time to clear the
courtroom of your monster.

83
00:04:45,560 --> 00:04:47,720
It's Deck Master's special ability.

84
00:04:49,880 --> 00:04:54,700
Yes, for the mere price of 1,000 life
points, I've left you defenseless.

85
00:04:55,120 --> 00:04:56,800
The verdict is in.

86
00:04:57,060 --> 00:04:58,100
You're finished.

87
00:05:01,220 --> 00:05:03,300
This case is coming to a close.

88
00:05:04,020 --> 00:05:05,497
It's not over yet, Johnson.

89
00:05:05,580 --> 00:05:07,457
I've placed two cards face down.

90
00:05:07,540 --> 00:05:08,500
So you do.

91
00:05:09,820 --> 00:05:10,650
Now...

92
00:05:10,733 --> 00:05:11,563
Hang in there.

93
00:05:14,120 --> 00:05:16,360
I play my plot of greed card.

94
00:05:16,840 --> 00:05:20,460
I bet you wish you'd drawn
this card, don't you, Joseph?

95
00:05:22,120 --> 00:05:22,950
Now,

96
00:05:23,033 --> 00:05:25,100
I'm able to draw two new cards,

97
00:05:25,300 --> 00:05:28,653
which is something that you
need to do quite desperately.

98
00:05:29,440 --> 00:05:32,240
Thanks to you, I can draw five cards now.

99
00:05:33,240 --> 00:05:35,680
Because I activate gamble!

100
00:05:38,140 --> 00:05:38,970
You see,

101
00:05:39,140 --> 00:05:40,977
I have no cards and you have six,

102
00:05:41,060 --> 00:05:45,680
which is exactly the combination I needed
in order to activate this trap card.

103
00:05:46,240 --> 00:05:47,070
Gamble?

104
00:05:48,100 --> 00:05:48,930
Yep.

105
00:05:49,013 --> 00:05:50,320
It's a risky card, Taya.

106
00:05:50,520 --> 00:05:53,697
But if it works, it can help Joey
turn this entire duel around,

107
00:05:53,780 --> 00:05:55,340
and it starts with a coin.

108
00:05:56,180 --> 00:05:58,840
And what exactly is so
risky about it, Yugi?

109
00:05:59,200 --> 00:06:01,440
Well, Joey flips a coin in the air.

110
00:06:01,660 --> 00:06:04,937
Then he calls heads or tails, and if
he's right, he gets to draw five cards.

111
00:06:05,020 --> 00:06:05,850
Ah.

112
00:06:05,933 --> 00:06:07,020
But if he's wrong,

113
00:06:07,480 --> 00:06:11,117
Joey's next turn gets skipped, And
he can't afford to let that happen.

114
00:06:11,200 --> 00:06:13,200
It could cost him the entire duel.

115
00:06:14,280 --> 00:06:18,920
He can take all the risks he wants,
because in my virtual courtroom,

116
00:06:19,200 --> 00:06:20,520
I control everything.

117
00:06:21,600 --> 00:06:22,430
Okay.

118
00:06:23,580 --> 00:06:26,000
This could make or break the game for me.

119
00:06:31,480 --> 00:06:33,774
Maybe this door will lead us back home.

120
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:36,900
Guess not.

121
00:06:38,460 --> 00:06:39,500
Huh. Oh, well.

122
00:06:39,740 --> 00:06:41,740
At least it's a change of scenery.

123
00:06:41,940 --> 00:06:42,940
Are you crazy?

124
00:06:43,180 --> 00:06:44,997
I don't want to be on a virtual beach,

125
00:06:45,080 --> 00:06:48,117
in a virtual forest, or even
in a virtual amusement park!

126
00:06:48,200 --> 00:06:49,540
I want out of here!

127
00:06:50,500 --> 00:06:51,480
Sorry, Seto.

128
00:06:51,660 --> 00:06:53,577
I just have to get that off my chest.

129
00:06:53,660 --> 00:06:56,600
This place is really
getting to me. Just relax.

130
00:06:57,000 --> 00:07:00,120
If you get upset, then
you're letting Noah win. Huh?

131
00:07:00,880 --> 00:07:02,460
Noah, show yourself!

132
00:07:02,860 --> 00:07:05,257
We're on to your little
game and it won't work!

133
00:07:05,340 --> 00:07:08,811
You think you can wear us down
by toying with our emotions,

134
00:07:09,080 --> 00:07:12,660
but you obviously don't know
who you're dealing with Really?

135
00:07:13,160 --> 00:07:19,720
I'd say I know exactly who I'm dealing
with Seto a no-good thief Now where was I?

136
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:20,830
Ah, yes.

137
00:07:20,960 --> 00:07:22,980
Come on, Joey. You can do this.

138
00:07:23,200 --> 00:07:25,400
You have a 50-50 chance

139
00:07:26,360 --> 00:07:27,560
Not exactly

140
00:07:29,460 --> 00:07:30,460
It's heads

141
00:07:31,200 --> 00:07:32,400
Come on

142
00:07:35,340 --> 00:07:36,760
Oh, no fair.

143
00:07:37,120 --> 00:07:38,760
No, not again.

144
00:07:39,260 --> 00:07:40,520
This is bad.

145
00:07:41,860 --> 00:07:46,331
When is this poor fool going to learn
that as long as we're in my courtroom,

146
00:07:46,600 --> 00:07:48,020
I control the outcome?

147
00:07:49,740 --> 00:07:53,040
It's still my turn, so I'll
reveal my face-down car.

148
00:07:54,100 --> 00:07:54,930
Scapegoat!

149
00:07:57,900 --> 00:08:00,720
Are those furballs
supposed to frighten me?

150
00:08:00,880 --> 00:08:03,617
I'll have them dismissed
from this trial in no time.

151
00:08:03,700 --> 00:08:05,600
This ought to do for starters.

152
00:08:06,220 --> 00:08:10,220
I'll play my Reinforcement
of the Army Magic card first,

153
00:08:10,500 --> 00:08:13,180
allowing me to add a warrior to my hand.

154
00:08:13,540 --> 00:08:16,360
Then I'll use polymerization.

155
00:08:16,700 --> 00:08:17,800
Know why, Joseph?

156
00:08:18,180 --> 00:08:22,420
To fuse together my R-Mail warrior
and my one-eyed shield dragon.

157
00:08:24,660 --> 00:08:27,140
Meet Dragoness, the Wicked Knight.

158
00:08:28,760 --> 00:08:30,860
Wow, big deal, Johnson.

159
00:08:31,100 --> 00:08:32,865
Your monster looks weak to me.

160
00:08:33,220 --> 00:08:35,840
But wait, thanks to
that magic card of his,

161
00:08:36,120 --> 00:08:38,697
Johnson can increase the
attack points of any monster

162
00:08:38,780 --> 00:08:41,839
that's made up of two other
monsters fused together.

163
00:08:42,640 --> 00:08:46,160
Time for my leading question
magic card to kick in.

164
00:08:46,540 --> 00:08:51,540
And power up my cameon wizard as
it tears down your first scapegoat.

165
00:08:53,520 --> 00:08:56,157
Now it will increase the
strength of my wicked

166
00:08:56,240 --> 00:08:58,980
knight as it eliminates
your second scapegoat.

167
00:09:03,800 --> 00:09:07,440
Two down, and two more scapegoats left.

168
00:09:07,700 --> 00:09:09,520
Not if I stop you first.

169
00:09:10,060 --> 00:09:10,890
Objection.

170
00:09:11,060 --> 00:09:12,420
Your turn is skipped.

171
00:09:12,820 --> 00:09:15,408
You called heads, but
you got tails, Joseph.

172
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:17,200
All right, then go.

173
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:18,840
As you wish.

174
00:09:19,240 --> 00:09:22,760
Now, time to destroy one more scapegoat.

175
00:09:25,860 --> 00:09:27,900
And last but not least,

176
00:09:28,100 --> 00:09:30,177
I'll enhance the strength
of my wicked knight

177
00:09:30,260 --> 00:09:33,380
once more and dismiss your last scapegoat.

178
00:09:35,380 --> 00:09:37,240
No, I'm done for.

179
00:09:39,300 --> 00:09:40,500
Case closed.

180
00:09:40,800 --> 00:09:42,440
Do you admit defeat? No.

181
00:09:42,980 --> 00:09:47,180
This duel won't be over until your
life points reach zero, Jansen.

182
00:09:47,500 --> 00:09:49,140
No way am I giving up.

183
00:09:49,920 --> 00:09:50,750
Ow.

184
00:09:51,040 --> 00:09:54,100
Note to self, do not
punch virtual railing.

185
00:09:54,640 --> 00:09:55,470
That's right.

186
00:09:55,640 --> 00:09:56,697
Don't give up, Joey.

187
00:09:56,780 --> 00:10:01,240
This bad luck of yours is bound to
change Because it can't get any worse.

188
00:10:02,920 --> 00:10:04,020
Hey, Taya, listen.

189
00:10:04,160 --> 00:10:07,160
As far as pep talks go,
this is not your best work.

190
00:10:07,280 --> 00:10:09,180
I'm running out of options here.

191
00:10:09,660 --> 00:10:10,700
Don't give up!

192
00:10:10,920 --> 00:10:13,685
There's something fishy
about this Johnson guy.

193
00:10:13,840 --> 00:10:17,546
It seems like more than just bad
luck that's holding Joey down.

194
00:10:17,960 --> 00:10:19,720
Yes, Yugi, I agree.

195
00:10:20,260 --> 00:10:21,090
Much more.

196
00:10:21,380 --> 00:10:24,217
Johnson is controlling the
outcome of Joey's moves.

197
00:10:24,300 --> 00:10:27,317
I've been sensing it since
the beginning of this duel.

198
00:10:27,400 --> 00:10:29,080
This judge is cheating.

199
00:10:29,300 --> 00:10:30,420
I knew it!

200
00:10:30,660 --> 00:10:34,320
We've got to step in, or Joey's
mind will be trapped here!

201
00:10:36,020 --> 00:10:37,980
Hey, check out that light!

202
00:10:40,680 --> 00:10:41,740
Wait a second!

203
00:10:42,080 --> 00:10:43,060
That's Noah!

204
00:10:46,220 --> 00:10:50,000
Master, what brings you
here? Silence! Yes, sir.

205
00:10:50,380 --> 00:10:52,400
Noah, it is him!

206
00:10:53,320 --> 00:10:56,820
This is even worse than that
never-ending virtual forest!

207
00:10:57,260 --> 00:10:58,201
Hold on, Mokuba!

208
00:10:58,960 --> 00:10:59,790
Huh?

209
00:10:59,873 --> 00:11:00,703
It's Noah.

210
00:11:01,380 --> 00:11:02,360
Time out!

211
00:11:02,700 --> 00:11:04,580
Stop the duel! Huh?

212
00:11:04,800 --> 00:11:05,920
What's the deal?

213
00:11:06,200 --> 00:11:08,860
Noah, you can't, sir. Please.

214
00:11:09,040 --> 00:11:13,080
I'm only a few moves away from
taking over this fool's body.

215
00:11:13,480 --> 00:11:15,760
You don't deserve that prize, Johnson.

216
00:11:16,020 --> 00:11:18,020
Not after what you just pulled.

217
00:11:18,980 --> 00:11:19,810
Huh?

218
00:11:19,893 --> 00:11:21,200
So, he is a cheater.

219
00:11:21,560 --> 00:11:23,120
Sad to say it's true.

220
00:11:23,400 --> 00:11:25,597
The Honorable Judge Man
is nothing but a fraud

221
00:11:25,680 --> 00:11:27,397
who's been cheating you
from the very beginning.

222
00:11:27,480 --> 00:11:31,620
He's been using my virtual technology
to tamper with your dice rolls.

223
00:11:31,920 --> 00:11:34,117
How about I tamper with your face, Mr.

224
00:11:34,200 --> 00:11:36,960
So-Called Man of Justice,
you big fat fake?

225
00:11:37,800 --> 00:11:40,520
But, Noah, I couldn't risk losing this.

226
00:11:40,840 --> 00:11:42,800
Please, you must understand me.

227
00:11:42,940 --> 00:11:46,517
I can't take living in this virtual
prison for one moment longer.

228
00:11:46,600 --> 00:11:47,430
It's torture.

229
00:11:47,580 --> 00:11:49,180
Your excuses bore me.

230
00:11:49,440 --> 00:11:53,037
I brought you five into my world
with the understanding that under

231
00:11:53,120 --> 00:11:56,944
my leadership you would defeat
Seto Kaiba and his little friends.

232
00:11:57,360 --> 00:12:01,600
But if you cheat, I can't prove that
I'm truly more deserving than him.

233
00:12:02,260 --> 00:12:03,240
Than me?

234
00:12:03,440 --> 00:12:05,020
More deserving of what?

235
00:12:05,260 --> 00:12:07,495
For years I've lived in Seto's shadow,

236
00:12:07,780 --> 00:12:10,397
always trying to prove
that I'm the better one.

237
00:12:10,480 --> 00:12:13,197
I should be the president
of Kaiba Corp., not him.

238
00:12:13,280 --> 00:12:15,357
And it's about time
I've proven to Gozaburo

239
00:12:15,440 --> 00:12:17,957
Kaiba that he should have
left the company to me.

240
00:12:18,040 --> 00:12:18,870
What?

241
00:12:18,953 --> 00:12:24,480
But my stepfather, Gozaburo, has been
missing without a trace for over five years!

242
00:12:25,100 --> 00:12:28,453
And why would Noah want to
prove something to him anyway?

243
00:12:28,780 --> 00:12:31,120
This kid is not who he seems to be.

244
00:12:31,460 --> 00:12:32,900
But who is he?

245
00:12:34,240 --> 00:12:35,420
Excuse me, boys.

246
00:12:35,680 --> 00:12:38,277
If I may interrupt this little
quarrel for just a second,

247
00:12:38,360 --> 00:12:40,017
the defendant would like to speak.

248
00:12:40,100 --> 00:12:44,040
If Johnson plays by the rules,
I may still be able to win this.

249
00:12:44,580 --> 00:12:46,698
Sorry, but this doesn't concern you.

250
00:12:47,420 --> 00:12:52,361
Johnson, it's time for me to do something
that I should have done the day I met you.

251
00:12:52,460 --> 00:12:55,280
Noah, please don't! Yoo-hoo.

252
00:12:56,020 --> 00:12:57,400
What? Look,

253
00:12:57,660 --> 00:13:02,417
I'm willing to forgive Judge Gruesome as
long as he agrees to duel fair and square.

254
00:13:02,500 --> 00:13:06,240
Noah, if he wins, you still
get to prove your strength.

255
00:13:06,520 --> 00:13:07,740
And if I win,

256
00:13:07,920 --> 00:13:10,077
I get to prove that Joey
Wheeler doesn't sit back

257
00:13:10,160 --> 00:13:12,997
and let freaky-looking
frauds get the best of him.

258
00:13:13,080 --> 00:13:13,910
Fine.

259
00:13:14,200 --> 00:13:18,080
Well, good luck, and I hope you
understand what you just did.

260
00:13:18,340 --> 00:13:20,620
The stakes of this duel still stand.

261
00:13:22,640 --> 00:13:24,560
Wow, sure beats the subway.

262
00:13:24,880 --> 00:13:26,860
All right, let's do this thing.

263
00:13:27,320 --> 00:13:29,120
You did hear Noah, right?

264
00:13:29,620 --> 00:13:34,700
You lose, and I still get to
escape by taking control of you.

265
00:13:35,020 --> 00:13:36,180
Yeah, I get it.

266
00:13:37,620 --> 00:13:38,450
Hmm,

267
00:13:38,533 --> 00:13:42,457
then I guess you are as foolish as you look
because you're about to lose everything,

268
00:13:42,540 --> 00:13:43,370
Joseph.

269
00:13:43,453 --> 00:13:45,740
and with your body under my jurisdiction,

270
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:48,937
your mind will be sentenced to wander this

271
00:13:49,020 --> 00:13:52,180
cyber universe for all
eternity without bail.

272
00:13:52,780 --> 00:13:55,420
You got me shaking in
my boots, Your Honor.

273
00:13:55,660 --> 00:13:56,780
You're real tough.

274
00:13:56,940 --> 00:13:59,881
But it's too bad you can't
cheat anymore, Johnson.

275
00:14:00,380 --> 00:14:01,210
Touché.

276
00:14:01,400 --> 00:14:03,300
Now let's finish this duel.

277
00:14:05,560 --> 00:14:07,760
Well, looky here.

278
00:14:08,120 --> 00:14:11,897
I think my luck is beginning
to change now. All right!

279
00:14:11,980 --> 00:14:15,420
Hot Agreed lets me draw two cards. Sweet!

280
00:14:15,860 --> 00:14:19,040
These two bad boys right
here are just what I need.

281
00:14:19,420 --> 00:14:21,980
And now it's time to move my Deck Master.

282
00:14:22,860 --> 00:14:23,690
Flameswordsman,

283
00:14:23,773 --> 00:14:28,217
go to the center of the playing field so
I can use you to attack this Creepazoid.

284
00:14:28,300 --> 00:14:31,653
But first, I'll boost your
power with Burning Soul Sword.

285
00:14:32,960 --> 00:14:34,380
Not so fast.

286
00:14:34,660 --> 00:14:38,366
You need to sacrifice a monster
for Burning Soul Sword to work.

287
00:14:38,960 --> 00:14:42,901
Hey, what makes you think I don't
know how my own magic card works?

288
00:14:43,160 --> 00:14:45,460
First, I have to sacrifice a monster,

289
00:14:45,720 --> 00:14:50,157
and then whichever creature's holding
the soul sword gets more attack points.

290
00:14:50,240 --> 00:14:52,652
In this case, that's my flamed swordsman.

291
00:14:52,980 --> 00:14:54,820
I stand corrected. However,

292
00:14:55,140 --> 00:14:57,537
you seem to have forgotten
one major fact about

293
00:14:57,620 --> 00:15:00,738
your strategy that will
prove to be most unfortunate,

294
00:15:00,860 --> 00:15:01,690
Joseph.

295
00:15:01,773 --> 00:15:02,657
Look at the field.

296
00:15:02,740 --> 00:15:07,640
You have no monsters left to Sacrifice,
you fool, so your plan won't work.

297
00:15:16,560 --> 00:15:18,000
I'm not through yet.

298
00:15:18,380 --> 00:15:21,000
I still got this little number left.

299
00:15:22,500 --> 00:15:25,300
My arduous decision magic card.

300
00:15:25,700 --> 00:15:26,960
Talk about risk.

301
00:15:27,220 --> 00:15:31,757
If this doesn't work, he could lose the
entire duel to Johnson right now, Taya.

302
00:15:31,840 --> 00:15:32,817
But how, Yugi?

303
00:15:32,900 --> 00:15:37,560
Playing that magic card allows Joey
to draw two more cards from his deck,

304
00:15:37,700 --> 00:15:39,700
and that's where things get tough.

305
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:43,294
Because then Johnson has to
pick one of those two cards.

306
00:15:43,420 --> 00:15:45,977
If he chooses a monster,
Joey can summon it.

307
00:15:46,060 --> 00:15:48,354
But if he chooses a magic or trap card,

308
00:15:48,500 --> 00:15:51,117
it goes to the graveyard
and Joey's turn is over.

309
00:15:51,200 --> 00:15:52,720
Well, your choice.

310
00:15:53,560 --> 00:15:55,560
If you haven't figured it out yet,

311
00:15:55,760 --> 00:15:58,877
the outcome of this entire
duel depends on this one move.

312
00:15:58,960 --> 00:16:01,277
And with Noah watching, you can't cheat,

313
00:16:01,360 --> 00:16:04,125
which means our fate will
be decided by chance.

314
00:16:04,680 --> 00:16:07,580
Your fate was sealed the moment we met.

315
00:16:07,860 --> 00:16:11,360
Just pick a card, Jansen, and
quit your stalling already.

316
00:16:11,600 --> 00:16:13,400
It's not a tough choice.

317
00:16:13,720 --> 00:16:15,073
There's only two cards.

318
00:16:15,360 --> 00:16:17,419
Of course, if you choose a monster,

319
00:16:17,520 --> 00:16:20,317
I can sacrifice it to
power up my flame swordsman

320
00:16:20,400 --> 00:16:22,977
and blast away the rest
of your life points.

321
00:16:23,060 --> 00:16:25,560
Yes, but if I choose a magic or trap card,

322
00:16:25,700 --> 00:16:28,876
then your swordsman remains
weak, and I'll destroy it,

323
00:16:29,020 --> 00:16:30,314
thus winning the duel.

324
00:16:30,900 --> 00:16:32,200
Come on, buddy.

325
00:16:32,400 --> 00:16:33,897
What are you gonna do here?

326
00:16:33,980 --> 00:16:36,140
Choose right or left hand.

327
00:16:36,420 --> 00:16:37,760
The time is now.

328
00:16:39,340 --> 00:16:40,980
Yeah, Joey, stay tough.

329
00:16:41,380 --> 00:16:43,040
Johnson is losing his cool.

330
00:16:43,320 --> 00:16:46,202
He'll never be able to
cheat his way out of this.

331
00:16:46,580 --> 00:16:50,640
That fool Wheeler is risking the
entire duel on a game of chance.

332
00:16:51,080 --> 00:16:52,786
Come on, pick a card already.

333
00:16:53,300 --> 00:16:55,980
All this suspense is driving me crazy.

334
00:16:56,720 --> 00:17:00,660
Well, if you can't take it, just
imagine how Joey feels right now.

335
00:17:03,120 --> 00:17:04,320
Let's do this.

336
00:17:04,780 --> 00:17:07,437
The more you put it off,
the harder it's going to be.

337
00:17:07,520 --> 00:17:09,200
Just pick a car, Jansen.

338
00:17:09,920 --> 00:17:11,240
All right, all right.

339
00:17:11,660 --> 00:17:13,240
Yeah, I'm waiting.

340
00:17:13,840 --> 00:17:15,780
I pick your left hand.

341
00:17:16,820 --> 00:17:18,200
Are you sure?

342
00:17:19,460 --> 00:17:21,540
I mean, really sure?

343
00:17:23,360 --> 00:17:24,280
I'm sure.

344
00:17:24,840 --> 00:17:26,797
That's an old trick, but a good one.

345
00:17:26,880 --> 00:17:30,580
However, I won't be fooled
by your childish antics.

346
00:17:30,760 --> 00:17:32,860
You asked me twice if I was sure.

347
00:17:33,100 --> 00:17:36,041
Your hesitation proves
I've made the right choice.

348
00:17:36,180 --> 00:17:37,160
If you say so.

349
00:17:37,440 --> 00:17:41,340
I've spent years and years convincing
people that lies were truth,

350
00:17:41,500 --> 00:17:43,737
so you have little
chance of outwitting me,

351
00:17:43,820 --> 00:17:44,650
Joseph.

352
00:17:44,860 --> 00:17:49,460
I'm positive I haven't picked your
monster card, so this case is closed.

353
00:17:50,640 --> 00:17:52,217
Judgment in favor of me.

354
00:17:52,300 --> 00:17:55,124
Now, please, show me the
card in your left hand.

355
00:17:55,320 --> 00:17:57,000
Oh, wait. Yeah?

356
00:17:57,700 --> 00:17:59,880
Uh, I changed my mind.

357
00:18:00,280 --> 00:18:01,780
The right hand, then?

358
00:18:03,460 --> 00:18:04,680
That's gotta hurt.

359
00:18:05,860 --> 00:18:07,360
Yeah! All right!

360
00:18:07,540 --> 00:18:10,775
You chose my monster card
known as Goblin Attack Force.

361
00:18:13,500 --> 00:18:14,560
So now,

362
00:18:14,700 --> 00:18:19,680
I'm able to sacrifice my goblins and add
their attack points to my Deckmaster,

363
00:18:19,860 --> 00:18:23,840
Flame Swordsman, Thanks to the
powers of my burning soul sword.

364
00:18:32,240 --> 00:18:37,860
All right, it's time for Flame Swordsman
to attack Dragonist, the Wicked Knight.

365
00:18:45,760 --> 00:18:47,680
No, this can't be.

366
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:49,437
I never lose in the courtroom.

367
00:18:49,520 --> 00:18:54,900
I once convinced a jury that a man who
was terrified of water stole a boat.

368
00:18:55,160 --> 00:18:57,240
How can I be fooled by some kid?

369
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:04,960
Oh, yeah!

370
00:19:05,560 --> 00:19:06,390
Look out!

371
00:19:06,480 --> 00:19:07,480
Who's the man?

372
00:19:07,860 --> 00:19:09,500
Way to go, Joey!

373
00:19:09,860 --> 00:19:12,300
That was awesome! Ha-ha! Yeah!

374
00:19:14,280 --> 00:19:16,997
Wait, we still have to
go find everyone else.

375
00:19:17,080 --> 00:19:20,797
Yeah, the other members of the Big
Five might be dueling them right now.

376
00:19:20,880 --> 00:19:22,540
Did you say dueling them?

377
00:19:23,360 --> 00:19:24,340
Who's dueling?

378
00:19:24,600 --> 00:19:26,660
They want to duel us all, Joey.

379
00:19:27,620 --> 00:19:29,117
Everyone who's trapped here.

380
00:19:29,200 --> 00:19:30,720
We are all in this.

381
00:19:30,940 --> 00:19:32,760
All of us! Stop, Joey!

382
00:19:32,980 --> 00:19:33,921
That's not fair!

383
00:19:34,180 --> 00:19:36,540
Serenity's never dueled before! No!

384
00:19:36,920 --> 00:19:39,817
We'll find her, Joey, and
we'll make sure she's okay.

385
00:19:39,900 --> 00:19:40,840
I promise.

386
00:19:41,300 --> 00:19:42,540
Let's get moving!

387
00:19:44,180 --> 00:19:45,540
I'm coming, Serenity!

388
00:19:46,120 --> 00:19:46,950
Wait!

389
00:19:47,033 --> 00:19:47,863
Wait for us!

390
00:19:47,946 --> 00:19:49,080
Come back, Joey! Please!
